// BASIC profile: is anything arriving at all? Run this first.
//
// WORKSPACE SCHEMA. A workspace-based Application Insights does NOT expose the
// classic tables when queried from the Log Analytics workspace: use AppMetrics,
// not customMetrics. The columns rename too, so a table-name-only swap still
// fails:
//     customMetrics    -> AppMetrics
//     timestamp        -> TimeGenerated
//     customDimensions -> Properties
//     value            -> Sum
//     valueCount       -> ItemCount
// customMetrics has NO `itemCount` column (that's a traces/requests/exceptions
// thing) - using it fails with SEM0100 'Failed to resolve scalar expression'.
// The classic names DO work from the Application Insights blade, which is why
// the other files in this folder read differently.
//
// EXPECTED for the BASIC policy pair:
//   copilot_byok_request                         (our emit-metric, one per call)
//   Prompt Tokens / Completion Tokens / Total Tokens   (llm-emit-token-metric)
//
// IF THIS RETURNS NOTHING but AppRequests shows traffic in the same window, the
// APIM 'applicationinsights' diagnostic is missing properties.metrics: true and
// emit-metric is being dropped silently. That is issue #16; see
// custom-metrics-smoke.kql for the gateway-trace confirmation.
AppMetrics
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| summarize Points = count(), Last = max(TimeGenerated) by Name
| order by Name asc
